# src/features/

Each subdirectory is an Event-Driven module following event sourcing patterns.

## Module structure

```
<moduleName>/
├── <moduleName>.routes.ts          ← manual DI — creates EventStore, Outbox, Projection, Handler, Controller, Router
├── commands/                       ← write operations
│   ├── create-<moduleName>.command.ts
│   └── create-<moduleName>.command-handler.ts
├── events/                         ← domain events (immutable data classes)
│   ├── <moduleName>-created.event.ts
│   ├── <moduleName>-updated.event.ts
│   └── <moduleName>-deleted.event.ts
├── aggregates/                     ← aggregate root
│   └── <moduleName>.aggregate.ts
├── projections/                    ← materialized read models
│   └── <moduleName>.projection.ts
├── event-store/                    ← append-only event log
│   └── event-store.ts
├── dto/                            ← request validation
│   └── create-<moduleName>.dto.ts
└── infrastructure/                 ← Koa adapters
    ├── <moduleName>.controller.ts
    └── outbox/
        └── outbox.ts               ← reliable event publishing queue
```

## Event sourcing flow

### Write path
1. Controller receives HTTP request, extracts DTO, builds command
2. Handler calls `Aggregate.create(name)` or `Aggregate.fromHistory(events)`
3. Aggregate produces events via domain methods (create, updateName, delete)
4. Handler calls `EventStore.append(aggregateId, type, events, expectedVersion)` — concurrency is checked
5. After successful append, handler updates the projection and enqueues events in the outbox
6. Aggregate marks events as committed

### Read path
1. Controller calls `Projection.findById(id)` or `Projection.findAll()`
2. Projection returns materialized data — never touches the event store

## Routing conventions

- `POST   /<module>`           → `controller.create`
- `GET    /<module>`           → `controller.findAll`
- `GET    /<module>/:id`       → `controller.findOne`
- `PATCH  /<module>/:id`       → `controller.update`
- `DELETE /<module>/:id`       → `controller.remove`

## Important rules

- Aggregates should never have side effects — they only produce events
- Projections are eventually consistent — they update synchronously after store append in this template
- Outbox is the single source for publishing events to external systems
- Event store is append-only — never modify or delete stored events
